    "held_on": "2007-04-30T14:00:00.000Z",
    "question_text": "Statement I The total translational kinetic energy of all the molecules of a given mass of an ideal gas is $1.5$ times the product of its pressure and its volume.\nStatement II The molecules of a gas collide with each other and the velocities of the molecules change due to the collision.",
    "question_image": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "xjNjG",
        "text": "\nStatement I is true, Statement II is true; Statement II is a correct explanation for Statement I\n",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "OgsJn",
        "text": "\nStatement I is true, Statement II is true; Statement II is NOT a correct explanation for Statement I\n",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "FUeGq",
        "text": "\nStatement I is true, Statement II is false\n",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "PnB0b",
        "text": "\nStatement I is false, Statement II is true",
        "image": null
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "OgsJn",
    "solution_text": "Total translational kinetic energy $=\\frac{3}{2} n R T=\\frac{3}{2} P V=1.5 P \\mathrm{~V}$\n$\\therefore$ Correct option is (b).",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Degree of Freedom and Specific Heat"
  },
